<%# KI-Pakete §7/§7.1 plus doc/ki_zugang_umbau_plan.md D6: what is true regardless of
    which way is open — the permanent "Aktuell" line, a switch already under way, and the
    two-way chooser itself.

    The page asks an EITHER/OR ("Systempaket or own configuration?") and used to answer it
    by showing both branches stacked: filters and card grid, and below them the custom
    card. Whoever answered that question for the first time had to work out that the last
    entry was an alternative to the list above it rather than a member of it.

    TWO SIGNALS, kept apart on purpose:
      open   — which pane is currently shown. Carried by the selection frame (border-2 +
               shadow, the Neo "selected" shape) and by aria-current.
      active — which way is IN FORCE. Carried by the small "Aktiv" chip.
    Separating them is what lets somebody look at the other way without the page claiming
    they already switched to it.

    Links, not a Stimulus controller, for the same reasons the filter rows are links (see
    _package_filter_row): the whole state is one query param, so it is bookmarkable,
    back-button-correct and directly assertable in a request spec.

    Tile ORDER is fixed, "Systempaket" first, and deliberately not sorted by what is
    active: stable geometry beats context sorting, and the chip already carries that
    information. %>
<h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-cream-900">
  <i class="bi bi-box-seam mr-2"></i>
  <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.title') %>
</h3>
<p class="mt-1 text-sm text-cream-700"><%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.intro') %></p>

<%# "Dauerhaft sichtbar in den KI-Einstellungen" (§7) — and deliberately OUTSIDE
    the filters: an org can sit on a package the strict default hides, or on one
    the operator has since unpublished. The line states what is true, the grid
    below is the catalogue. %>
<div class="mt-4 border border-cream-300 rounded-lg bg-cream-100 p-4">
  <% if @current_package.present? %>
    <p class="text-sm font-bold text-cream-900">
      <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.current_label_package',
            name: @current_package.name, description: @current_package.description) %>
    </p>
    <% if @current_package.processing_region.present? %>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-cream-700">
        <i class="bi bi-geo-alt mr-1"></i>
        <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.card.processing_region',
              region: @current_package.processing_region) %>
      </p>
    <% end %>
  <% elsif @organisation.ai_custom_access_configured? %>
    <p class="text-sm font-bold text-cream-900">
      <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.current_label_custom') %>
    </p>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-cream-700">
      <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.current_custom_hint') %>
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <%# Z3 (D7): no package AND no credentials. The line said "Aktuell: Eigene
        Konfiguration" here, which named a decision nobody had made — the schema cannot
        tell "never chose" from "chose custom", and the line believed the schema. It says
        what is TRUE instead, and what to do about it. Same neutral box, no green. %>
    <p class="text-sm font-bold text-cream-900">
      <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.none_configured_title') %>
    </p>
    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-cream-700">
      <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.none_configured_hint') %>
    </p>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# P4c: directly under the "Aktuell" line, because a switch underway is a statement
    ABOUT that line — the package named above is the one being switched TO, while
    the search still reads from the old space until the flip.

    ABOVE the chooser, not inside a pane: it holds whichever way is open. %>
<%= render 'organisations/ai_settings/switch_progress' %>

<div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2" id="ai_package_chooser">
  <%# ⚠️ The custom tile's chip asks TWO things, not one (D7). A blank ai_package_id means
      "own configuration" by convention (E1-C) and says nothing about whether credentials
      exist — asking only that gave a fresh organisation an "Aktiv" chip on a way nobody
      had chosen and nothing was behind. Organisation#ai_custom_access_configured? is the
      one owner of the second half. %>
  <%
    modes = [
      [Organisations::AiSettingsController::MODE_PACKAGES, 'packages', 'box-seam',
       @organisation.ai_package_id.present?],
      [Organisations::AiSettingsController::MODE_CUSTOM, 'custom', 'key',
       @organisation.ai_package_id.blank? && @organisation.ai_custom_access_configured?]
    ]
  %>
  <% modes.each do |mode, key, icon, in_force| %>
    <% open_pane = @package_mode == mode %>
    <%= link_to organisation_ai_settings_path(@organisation,
                                              provider_scope: @package_provider_scope,
                                              processing_scope: @package_processing_scope,
                                              package_mode: mode,
                                              anchor: 'ai_package_chooser'),
                class: "block rounded-lg p-4 transition-transform hover:-translate-y-0.5 #{
                  open_pane ? 'border-2 border-ink bg-cream-50 shadow-[3px_3px_0_0_#000000]'
                            : 'border border-cream-300 bg-surface-raised'
                }",
                aria: { current: open_pane ? 'true' : nil } do %>
      <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
        <h4 class="text-base font-bold text-cream-900">
          <i class="bi bi-<%= icon %> mr-2 text-cream-600"></i>
          <%= t("views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.chooser.#{key}_title") %>
        </h4>
        <% if in_force %>
          <%# data-chooser-chip, same idea as the hub's data-card-state: the chip is a
              DECISION, and a spec should be able to ask which tile carries it without
              matching on a word that also occurs inside "aktiviert" elsewhere on the
              page. %>
          <span class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center rounded border border-ink bg-ink px-2 py-1 text-xs font-bold text-cream-50"
                data-chooser-chip="<%= key %>">
            <%= t('views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.chooser.active_chip') %>
          </span>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-cream-700">
        <%= t("views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.chooser.#{key}_subline") %>
      </p>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>
